WEBVTT

00:00:00.015 --> 00:00:03.541
Easy Greek Myths. Persephone and the Seasons.

00:00:03.541 --> 00:00:06.196
Demeter was the goddess of the fields.

00:00:06.196 --> 00:00:09.321
She made the corn grow and the fruit trees flower.

00:00:09.321 --> 00:00:14.039
She had a daughter named Persephone, whom she loved more than anything.

00:00:14.039 --> 00:00:17.495
One day Persephone was picking flowers in a field.

00:00:17.495 --> 00:00:19.301
Suddenly the ground opened.

00:00:19.301 --> 00:00:24.843
Out came Hades, the king of the dead, in a black cart pulled by black horses.

00:00:24.843 --> 00:00:28.352
He had seen Persephone and wanted her to be his queen.

00:00:28.352 --> 00:00:33.253
He pulled her into his cart and took her down to his dark country under the earth.

00:00:33.253 --> 00:00:35.933
Demeter looked for her daughter everywhere.

00:00:35.933 --> 00:00:39.044
She walked over the whole world for many days.

00:00:39.044 --> 00:00:42.104
She was so sad that she forgot the fields.

00:00:42.104 --> 00:00:43.318
Nothing grew.

00:00:43.318 --> 00:00:45.600
The leaves fell from the trees.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:49.994
The ground became cold and hard, and people had nothing to eat.

00:00:49.994 --> 00:00:56.342
At last Zeus, the king of the gods, said, "This must stop, or everyone will die."

00:00:56.342 --> 00:01:00.099
He sent a message to Hades: "Let Persephone go."

00:01:00.099 --> 00:01:01.637
But there was a rule.

00:01:01.637 --> 00:01:05.777
Anyone who ate food in the country of the dead had to stay there.

00:01:05.777 --> 00:01:09.373
And Persephone had eaten six small red seeds.

00:01:09.373 --> 00:01:11.013
So Zeus decided.

00:01:11.013 --> 00:01:16.870
For six months of every year, one for each seed, Persephone must live with Hades.

00:01:16.870 --> 00:01:19.999
For the other six months she could live with her mother.

00:01:19.999 --> 00:01:23.867
When Persephone comes back to the earth, Demeter is happy.

00:01:23.867 --> 00:01:26.895
The flowers open and the fields turn green.

00:01:26.895 --> 00:01:28.784
That is spring and summer.

00:01:28.784 --> 00:01:34.415
When her daughter goes down again, Demeter is sad, and the earth turns cold.

00:01:34.415 --> 00:01:36.306
That is autumn and winter.

00:01:36.306 --> 00:01:39.314
This is how the Greeks explained the seasons.
